From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muhammad Jagot <MoJagotasdfgh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:03:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fork 001: sites plug-in slot (the four built-in site readers
 out)

What: internal/sources/sites.go becomes an empty plug-in slot (SiteReader,
RegisterSite); the Knaben, TorrentsCSV, SubsPlease and IPTorrents readers,
their tests and their fixtures are removed. The add form hides the "site"
choice while nothing is plugged in, and the messages no longer name the
four sites. Site.NoFeed replaces the one TorrentsCSV special case.

Why: this build ships no sites or trackers; the owner plugs in his own
readers (a Go file in internal/sources that calls RegisterSite from init())
or uses the Prowlarr/Jackett bridge. The "site" Source format, its routes
and its stored rows stay as they are, so a reader plugged in later works
with Sources added before.

Undo: revert this one commit, or leave this patch out of fork/patches.

Check: internal/sources/fork_check_001_test.go (no built-in reader, the add
route refuses a site that is not plugged in, the slot reaches a plugged-in
reader for caps, search, test); apply.ps1 also scans holyarrs-mod.exe for
the four sites' addresses.

Upstream files edited: internal/sources/{sites.go, sites_test.go,
test_failed_test.go, service.go, routes_sources.go},
frontend/src/lib/sources/api.ts, routes/settings/sources/+page.svelte, and the JSON-key snapshot
tools/structurecheck/testdata/json-keys.txt (the readers' keys out,
no_feed in);
internal/sources/testdata/sites removed. No database migration.

Needs: none
